course: dictionary
lesson: 10843
title: Many versions of one thing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A version is one form of something that is a little different from other forms of it. «A new version of the game» means the same game, changed or improved a little. Ask yourself: is this the same thing, but made or told a different way?
explain: A version can also be one person's account of what happened. «His version of events» is the story he tells about what happened. Two people can see the same event and tell it differently, so their versions may not match. When that happens, look for evidence, such as photos or witnesses, to find out what really happened.
explain: A version can be a story, song or film told or made again in a different way. «A modern version of Cinderella» is still Cinderella, but it is told in a new style. Check your meaning: if you can swap in "a different form of" and the sentence still makes sense, you have it right.
fact: A version is one form of something, a little different from other forms of it.
fact: A version can be one person's account of what happened, such as «his version of events».
fact: A version can be a story, song or film told or made again in a different way, such as «the film version».
fact: «The latest version» means the newest form of something, like software you update.
fact: Edvard Munch made several versions of The Scream from 1893.
exercise: «The same seed in the same game version gives the same numbers.» What is a game version? | *A different form of the same game | A kind of computer screen | A prize for winning the game | A player who plays the game for hours
exercise: «A draft is a version of your writing that you plan to improve.» What is a draft? | A rule that everyone must follow | A kind of pen for writing neatly | *An early form of your writing that you plan to improve | A finished book sold in a shop
exercise: Ella says, «I want the latest version.» What does latest version mean? | *The newest form of something | The cheapest copy in the shop | The longest film of all | The oldest story ever told
test: «Tom gave his version of events, but Sam had a different version.» What does version mean here? | A song sung again in a new way | A rule for playing fair | A kind of map | *One person's account of what happened
test: «He taught a version of the golden rule.» What does version mean here? | A prize for the best answer | A test he set the class | *A form of the golden rule, said in his own way | A picture of a golden crown
exam: Jayden reads, «Edvard Munch made several versions of The Scream from 1893.» What does several versions mean? | Several pictures of different people | Several copies of one picture, exactly the same | A single painting, finished in 1893 | *Several different forms of the same picture
